[
  {
    "id": "sitl36-tab",
    "type": "tab",
    "label": "SITL 26 Peer table in flight",
    "disabled": false,
    "info": "Fly ArduPilot sysid 1, then snapshot the Connection peer table (§8). Suite fires Start (GUIDED→arm→takeoff→velocity stream) then Snapshot after a long gap. Hard field asserts live in sitl/measure-peer-table.js; this example is the flow-level regression.",
    "env": []
  },
  {
    "id": "sitl36-comment",
    "type": "comment",
    "z": "sitl36-tab",
    "name": "Peer table enrichment while airborne",
    "info": "Chain: GUIDED (confirm) → Arm (confirm) → SET_MESSAGE_INTERVAL for GLOBAL_POSITION_INT / GPS_RAW_INT / SYS_STATUS → Takeoff 10 m (complete) → Move velocity stream north 1.5 m/s for 8 s.\n\nIntervals matter: completion and the peer table need GLOBAL_POSITION_INT; without an explicit request this SITL often leaves position null and takeoff times out with \"no position data\".\n\nSecond inject: mavlink-state snapshot → debug \"peer-table snapshot\". Expect armed:true, position.relativeAlt, gps.fixType, battery, home.\n\nConnection: bind 0.0.0.0:14550 → remote 127.0.0.1:14551, sysid 1.\n\nAuthoritative field checklist: node sitl/measure-peer-table.js (AP + PX4).",
    "x": 250,
    "y": 40,
    "wires": []
  },
